{
  "$comment": [
    "Deterministic grounded-retrieval evaluation corpus for the approved CASPEL",
    "RAG corpus (Corporate + ERP only). Every expected page was read off the",
    "indexed chunk text, not guessed.",
    "",
    "Two facts about this corpus drive most of the case design:",
    "  1. The ERP deck is written in Azerbaijani. Only page 1 carries English.",
    "     An English or Chinese question about ERP therefore has to cross a",
    "     language boundary, which is why dense retrieval stays authoritative",
    "     and why English stemming would be the wrong FTS configuration.",
    "  2. There is exactly one chunk per page, and a slide's text is short.",
    "     A whole-slide vector is an average of everything on the slide, which",
    "     is why cosine scores cluster inside a ~0.05 band for any question",
    "     about a document the deck covers.",
    "",
    "Split: 'tune' may be inspected while iterating. 'accept' is the fixed",
    "acceptance set and must not be consulted while tuning."
  ],
  "documents": {
    "caspel": "CASPEL Corporate Presentation",
    "erp": "CASPEL ERP Presentation"
  },
  "cases": [
